    "description": "Share of residents who are Hispanic or Latino of any race, pale apricot to burnt orange. Measured over all 5,806,512 blocks with a published value: 6 classes with breaks at 2%/6%/15%/30%/60%, which fall at the 40th/51st/68th/82nd/92nd percentile of the national distribution. 28.97% have no published value and draw in neutral gray rather than as a low value.",
